    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d891">

                <pb facs="0837" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Turkey/981: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-14T23:00:00+02:00">April 14, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 14—4:48 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>664. The Minister for Foreign Affairs has now agreed to reduce to 4,200 tons
                    monthly the deliveries of chrome to Germany. This is approximately 50 percent of
                    the rate at which deliveries have been made during recent months. He has also
                    agreed to substantially increase deliveries for British account to the
                    accessible ports.</p>
                <p>In view of the foregoing and particularly by reason of the nature of the joint
                    declaration which the British Ambassador and I are presenting to the Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs today concerning the delivery of strategic materials to
                    Germany by Turkey it would seem that delivery of the President’s proposed letter
                    to President Inonu would serve no useful purpose.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d891-f1"
                    /> For the Department’s information the letter was received today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
